# The tier budgets held above the start of the tests' processes (the owner's
# decision of 2026-11-13, docs/steps/11/answered.md): what the tier report
# of `xtask` computes, broken one rule at a time.

[break] budget-held-to-the-raw-total
rule: A tier is held to its budget by its total above the start of its tests' processes, not by its raw total.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: summarise
find: let verdict = verdict(above_start, budget);
replace: let verdict = verdict(seconds, budget);
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_slow_runner_alone_does_not_put_a_tier_over_its_budget

[break] start-cost-is-the-quickest-test
rule: The start cost is the time one in a hundred of the run's unit and integration tests beat, not the single quickest, which one lucky test moves.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: start_of
find: times[times.len() * START_PERCENTILE / 100]
replace: times[0]
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::the_start_cost_is_what_one_in_a_hundred_unit_and_integration_tests_beat

[break] system-tests-measure-the-start
rule: System tests are not looked at for the start cost: they start other processes of their own.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: start_of
find: .filter(|case| Tier::of(&case.binary, &case.name) != Tier::System)
replace: .filter(|_| true)
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::the_start_cost_is_what_one_in_a_hundred_unit_and_integration_tests_beat

[break] a-quick-test-counts-below-nothing
rule: A test quicker than the start cost counts as nothing, not as less than nothing.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: total
find: (case.seconds - start).max(0.0)
replace: (case.seconds - start)
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_test_quicker_than_the_start_cost_counts_as_nothing

[break] the-start-is-not-taken-off
rule: Each test's time is taken above the start cost before it is added to its tier.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: total
find: (case.seconds - start).max(0.0)
replace: case.seconds
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_test_quicker_than_the_start_cost_counts_as_nothing
    tiers::tests::a_slow_runner_alone_does_not_put_a_tier_over_its_budget
    tiers::tests::the_report_of_a_fixed_run_is_exactly_this
